## Report
Built a minimal PoC binary (crates/server/src/bin/panic_header.rs) that percent-decodes a response-content-type query parameter containing %0d%0a, sets it as Content-Type, and calls s3_response_to_hyper. The code path shows query_param uses percent_decode without filtering control characters (crates/server/src/http/request.rs:92-139), apply_response_overrides inserts query values into headers without validation (crates/server/src/http/mod.rs:561-576), and s3_response_to_hyper iterates headers then calls .expect(...) on the response builder (crates/server/src/http/mod.rs:541-549). Because the build requires libisal, I used a fake libisal via PKG_CONFIG_PATH to compile. Running the PoC triggered a panic with http::Error(InvalidHeaderValue), confirming the DoS via invalid header value.

